
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brett Terpstra recently shipped <a href="https://terminalwidget.app">TerminalWidget</a>, a useful, nerdy little utility right in line with that we&#8217;ve all come to love from Brett.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TerminalWidget takes the output from a shell script, a Shortcut, an AppleScript, or a plain URL, and turns it into a widget sitting on your Desktop or Home Screen. Sales numbers, backup status, network speed, a GitHub contribution graph. Whatever you can script, you can now glance at without opening a terminal window or a browser tab. It&#8217;s a universal purchase for $19.99, covering Mac, iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch, and it&#8217;s available now on the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/terminalwidget/id6764288419">App Store</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;m looking forward to digging in on it.</p>
